-- title:
--   Supersingular U_ℓ matrix equals class-set Hecke matrix, ℓ ∣ N
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q' \ge 5$, algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $q'$-torsion points vanish, and let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring exactly when $q' \in v$. Let $\Lambda_1 \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a maximal order (an order: contains $1$, multiplicatively closed, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning, finitely generated; maximal among orders) and $\theta_1$ an injective ring map from the subring of $\mathrm{End}$ of the base-changed curve generated by rationally represented endomorphisms onto $\Lambda_1$. Let $N \ge 1$ with $q' \nmid N$, and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $m$ and $N m^{-1}$ in the adelic box of $\Lambda_1$ (the additive group generated by $z \otimes \alpha$, $z \in \Lambda_1$, $\alpha$ an integral adele) and with the conjugate $m \hat{\Lambda}_1 m^{-1} \cap \mathbb{H}$ again maximal; put $R = \Lambda_1 \sqcap \mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,m$, assumed of relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive groups. Let $e$ be a bijection from the double coset set $\mathbb{H}^\times \backslash (\mathbb{H} \otimes \mathbb{A}^{\mathrm{fin}})^\times / \widehat{R}^\times$ (the stabiliser of the adelic box of $R$) onto the set of supersingular places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,N$ (rational, affine geometric places whose value at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q' κ`), and assume the adaptedness hypothesis $h_e$: for every idele $x$, every elliptic $W$, every nonzero rationally represented $\chi : X_1 \to W$ and unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}$ with $\theta_1$ carrying the kernel-ideal set of $\chi$ onto the conjugate-image of $d \cdot \mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,x$, and every $W'$ with rationally represented $\psi : W \to W'$, $\psi' : W' \to W$ satisfying $\psi' \psi = N$, $\psi \psi' = N$, kernel-ideal set of $\psi \circ \chi$ matching $d \cdot \mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,(xm)$, and $\ker \psi$ cyclic of order $N$, the valuation subring of $e$ of the class of $x$ is the pullback, along the inclusion of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,N$ into the full modular function field, of the valuation subring of $\mathrm{moduliPlace}\,\kappa\,N\,W\,(\ker\psi)$. Finally let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq q'$ and $\ell \mid N$, with the two degeneracy maps $\mathrm{heckeAlphaC}$ and $\mathrm{heckeBetaC}$ into the roof field integral. Then for all classes $i,j$ the $(e\,i, e\,j)$ entry of $\mathrm{ssHeckeMatrixC}\,q'\,\kappa\,N\,\ell$ — the sum over places $W$ of the roof $\mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,\kappa\,N\,\ell$ restricting to $e\,j$ along $\beta$ and to $e\,i$ along $\alpha$ of the product of the ramification index along $\beta$ with the residue degree along $\alpha$ — equals the $(i,j)$ entry of $\mathrm{classSetHeckeMatrix}$ for $\widehat{R}^\times$ and the set $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,R\,\ell$ of ideles $h$ lying in the prime Hecke set of $R$ at $\ell$ (that is, $h$ and $\ell h^{-1}$ in the box of $R$ while $h^{-1}$ and $\ell^{-1}h$ are not) which in addition do not normalise $R$ and for which $R \not\le \mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,h$; that entry is the cardinality of the Hecke incidence set at $(j,i)$.
--
--   This is the Čerednik–Drinfel'd style comparison of the $U_\ell$ correspondence on the supersingular points of $X_0(N)$ in characteristic $q'$ with the corresponding Brandt-type matrix on the class set of the Eichler order $R = \Lambda_1 \cap m\hat\Lambda_1m^{-1}$, for a prime $\ell$ dividing the level, the Hecke set being the $U_\ell$ double coset oriented at the vertex $\Lambda_1 = \mathrm{End}\,X_1$. It is used in the construction of a single bijection between the class set and the supersingular places intertwining all degeneracy Hecke operators.
